    "<a id=\"section-4\"></a>\n",
    "### **Section 4: ConvNet Architecture (2 points)**\n",
    "\n",
    "In this section, you will implement a convolutional neural network inspired by the structure of [LeNet-5](https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/726791). The network processes color images using three convolutional layers followed by two fully connected layers. Since you need to feed color images into this network, determine the kernel size of the first convolutional layer. Additionally, calculate the number of trainable parameters in the \"F6\" layer, providing the calculation process."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "05ee9888",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<span style=\"color:red\"><b><<<<<<< local</b></span>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class ConvNet(nn.Module):\n",
    "\n",
    "    def __init__(self, input_size, num_classes):\n",
    "        '''\t\n",
    "        Initializes the convolutional neural network model.\n",
    "\n",
    "        Args:\n",
    "            None\n",
    "        '''\n",
    "\n",
    "        # YOUR CODE HERE\n",
    "        super(ConvNet, self).__init__()\n",
    "        self.relu = nn.ReLU()\n",
    "        \n",
    "        self.conv1 = nn.Conv3d(input_size, 28, 5)\n",
    "        self.avgPool1 = nn.AvgPool3d(2, stride=2)\n",
    "        self.conv2 = nn.Conv3d(14, 10, 5)\n",
    "        self.avgPool2 = nn.AvgPool3d(2, stride=2)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # TODO: connection between convolutional and linear layers, flatten layer perhaps?\n",
    "        \n",
    "        self.lin1 = nn.Linear(120, 84)\n",
    "        self.softmax = nn.Softmax()\n",
    "        self.lin2 = nn.Linear(84, num_classes)\n",
    "\n",
    "    def forward(self, x):\n",
    "        '''\n",
    "        Defines the forward pass of the neural network.\n",
    "\n",
    "        Args:\n",
    "            x (torch.Tensor): The input tensor.\n",
    "\n",
    "        Returns:\n",
    "            torch.Tensor: The output tensor.\n",
    "        '''\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # YOUR CODE HERE\n",
    "        x = self.relu(self.conv1(x))\n",
    "        x = self.avgPool1(x)\n",
    "        x = self.relu(self.conv2(x))\n",
    "        x = self.avgPool2(x)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # TODO: connection between convolutional and linear layers, flatten layer perhaps?\n",
    "        \n",
    "        x = self.relu(self.lin1(x))\n",
    "        class_probs = self.softmax(self.lin2(x))\n",
    "        \n",
    "        return class_probs"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a3c2de3e",
   "metadata": {},
